{"request":["contract.json",{"pointer":"/conclusion"}],"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"contract.json\", \"pointer\": \"/conclusion\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"statement\": \"For every r>0 the function x↦e(x,r) is Lebesgue integrable on V; E is differentiable on (0,∞), and E'(r)=0 for every r>0. In particular E(s)=E(t) for all s,t>0. The energy is ∫_V (|u_t|^2+sum_{j=1}^n|u_j|^2) dx, with no factor 1/2 and no assertion at time zero.\", \"type\": \"(∀ r : ℝ, 0 < r → Integrable (fun x => e u x r)) ∧\\nDifferentiableOn ℝ (energy u) (Set.Ioi 0) ∧\\n(∀ r : ℝ, 0 < r → deriv (energy u) r = 0) ∧\\n(∀ s t : ℝ, 0 < s → 0 < t → energy u s = energy u t)\"}, \"has_more\": false, \"next_offset\": null}"}}
{"request":["contract.json",{"pointer":"/representation"}],"result":{"status":"fulfilled","value":"{\"id\": \"contract.json\", \"pointer\": \"/representation\", \"view\": \"string\", \"offset\": 0, \"end_offset\": 1431, \"total_chars\": 1431, \"has_more\": false, \"next_offset\": null, \"value\": \"Space V n is Fin n → ℝ, carrying its finite-product topology and product Lebesgue volume. Its Mathlib sup norm is used only as an auxiliary compatible finite-dimensional norm; source Euclidean coordinate topology, compactness and derivatives are unchanged, and source Euclidean norm expressions on spatial vectors are not replaced by this sup norm. Target W m is EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)=PiLp 2 with the Euclidean L² norm and inner product sum of coordinate products. Fin n enumerates source coordinates 1,...,n by j.val+1. u is total on V×ℝ; all assumptions and conclusions concern t>0, and restriction/extension on this open domain leaves derivatives unchanged. ContDiffOn ℝ ∞ means smooth to every finite order; scoped ∞ is (⊤:ℕ∞) coerced to WithTop ℕ∞, whereas the top of WithTop ℕ∞ is analytic order ω. All derivatives are total deriv/fderiv, zero if absent; smoothness at positive times justifies their ordinary meaning. Iterated Fréchet derivative vanishing in N002 is equivalent to all positive-order coordinate partials vanishing by evaluating the multilinear map on the finite spatial/time coordinate basis. fields enumerates exactly e,et,A,Bj,Tj,gj,dgj; membership carries no theorem. energy is a total Bochner integral expression; T003 supplies the guard that it is the finite Lebesgue energy on positive times. No M ports or background-note premise ports are needed. H003 is retained though unused in the source route.\"}"}}
