{"id":"source-map.json","pointer":"/roots","view":"value","value":[{"id":"H001","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"n and m are integers with n≥1 and m≥1 (represented as natural-number dimensions)."},{"id":"H002","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"u:R^n×(0,∞)→R^m is jointly smooth: every finite-order coordinate partial derivative exists and is continuous on this open domain."},{"id":"H003","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"q∈R^m is fixed and |q|=1."},{"id":"H004","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"For every x∈R^n and every r>0, |u(x,r)|=1."},{"id":"H005","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"For every x∈R^n and every r>0 there exists a real scalar a with u_tt(x,r)−Δu(x,r)=a u(x,r). No regularity or globally chosen scalar field is assumed."},{"id":"H006","kind":"hypothesis","statement":"For every pair of real numbers 0<s<t<∞ there exists a compact set C_[s,t]⊂R^n such that u(x,r)=q for every x∉C_[s,t] and every r∈[s,t]."},{"id":"M001","kind":"mathlib","statement":"For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed ring Z with a normed 𝕜-algebra structure, maps φ,ψ:𝕜→Z, point z∈𝕜 and vectors φ',ψ'∈Z: if φ has derivative φ' at z and ψ has derivative ψ' at z, then their pointwise product has derivative φ' ψ(z)+φ(z) ψ' at z. Here having derivative is the usual first-order difference-quotient limit.","source":{"declaration":"HasDerivAt.mul","hypotheses":["𝕜 is a nontrivially normed field; Z is a normed ring with a normed 𝕜-algebra structure.","φ has derivative φ' at z.","ψ has derivative ψ' at z."],"statement":"For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed ring Z with a normed 𝕜-algebra structure, maps φ,ψ:𝕜→Z, point z∈𝕜 and vectors φ',ψ'∈Z: if φ has derivative φ' at z and ψ has derivative ψ' at z, then their pointwise product has derivative φ' ψ(z)+φ(z) ψ' at z. Here having derivative is the usual first-order difference-quotient limit.","module":"Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Mul","signature":"@HasDerivAt.mul : ∀ {𝕜 : Type u} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField.{u} 𝕜] {x : 𝕜} {𝔸 : Type u_3} [inst_1 : NormedRing.{u_3} 𝔸]
  [inst_2 : NormedAlgebra.{u, u_3} 𝕜 𝔸] {c d : 𝕜 → 𝔸} {c' d' : 𝔸},
  HasDerivAt.{u, u_3} c c' x →
    HasDerivAt.{u, u_3} d d' x →
      HasDerivAt.{u, u_3} (HMul.hMul.{max u u_3, max u u_3, max u u_3} c d)
        (HAdd.hAdd.{u_3, u_3, u_3} (HMul.hMul.{u_3, u_3, u_3} c' (d x)) (HMul.hMul.{u_3, u_3, u_3} (c x) d')) x","declaration_kind":"theorem","mathlib_commit":"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c","source_path":"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/Deriv/Mul.lean","source_sha256":"1b6c653faf5b8a9f37d6f40786dd8451bde7007b675c46c58b420aa89a38bbad","evidence":[{"path":"library/M001-0002/library-sources.json","sha256":"003b168233abe70b35151de6291691d50918528475ba85e025ec58cfb599215d"}]}},{"id":"M002","kind":"mathlib","statement":"For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed additive commutative groups X,Z with normed 𝕜-vector-space structures, map φ:X→Z, point z∈X and smoothness order ℓ∈WithTop(N∞): if φ is C^ℓ at z and minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ, then its second Fréchet derivative is symmetric: for all v,w∈X, D(Dφ)(z)[v][w]=D(Dφ)(z)[w][v]. The minimum smoothness is 2 when the field has IsRCLikeNormedField (a real- or complex-like normed field) and analytic order ω otherwise; D denotes the total Fréchet derivative, zero when no derivative exists.","source":{"declaration":"ContDiffAt.isSymmSndFDerivAt","hypotheses":["The field and both normed spaces have the stated structures.","φ is C^ℓ at z.","minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ."],"module":"Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Symmetric","signature":"@ContDiffAt.isSymmSndFDerivAt : ∀ {𝕜 : Type u_1} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField.{u_1} 𝕜] {E : Type u_2} {F : Type u_3}
