  [inst_4 : NormedSpace.{u_1, u_3} 𝕜 F] {f : E → F} {x : E} {n : WithTop.{0} ℕ∞},
  ContDiffAt.{u_1, u_2, u_3} 𝕜 n f x → LE.le.{0} (minSmoothness.{u_1} 𝕜 2) n → IsSymmSndFDerivAt.{u_1, u_2, u_3} 𝕜 f x","declaration_kind":"theorem","mathlib_commit":"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c","source_path":"Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/FDeriv/Symmetric.lean","source_sha256":"c262fa67a6097d95f55ef053fb2870a9b84b097f21c8cfea65b46e6d1677d725","evidence":[{"path":"library/M002-0001/library-sources.json","sha256":"69fb653c43a766c0d13ab081230621ee5d1e2569bcf1c9c6c283276fed01e642"}],"statement":"For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed additive commutative groups X,Z with normed 𝕜-vector-space structures, map φ:X→Z, point z∈X and smoothness order ℓ∈WithTop(N∞): if φ is C^ℓ at z and minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ, then its second Fréchet derivative is symmetric: for all v,w∈X, D(Dφ)(z)[v][w]=D(Dφ)(z)[w][v]. The minimum smoothness is 2 when the field has IsRCLikeNormedField (a real- or complex-like normed field) and analytic order ω otherwise; D denotes the total Fréchet derivative, zero when no derivative exists."}},{"id":"M003","kind":"mathlib"…2261 tokens truncated…X×Y→Z integrable for μ×ν, ∫_{X×Y} φ d(μ×ν)=∫_X(∫_Y φ(z,w) dν(w)) dμ(z).","source":{"declaration":"MeasureTheory.integral_prod","hypotheses":["The measurable spaces, s-finite measures and real normed codomain have the stated structures.","φ is integrable for μ×ν."],"statement":"Let X,Y be measurable spaces, μ,ν measures on them which are s-finite, and Z a normed additive commutative group and normed real vector space. For any φ:X×Y→Z integrable for μ×ν, ∫_{X×Y} φ d(μ×ν)=∫_X(∫_Y φ(z,w) dν(w)) dμ(z).","module":"Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.Prod","signature":"@MeasureTheory.integral_prod : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {E : Type u_3} [inst : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α] [inst_1 : MeasurableSpace.{u_2} β]
