      (∫ (x : α), ∫ (y : β), f (Prod.mk.{u_1, u_2} x y) ∂ν ∂μ)","declaration_kind":"theorem","mathlib_commit":"905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c","source_path":"Mathlib/MeasureTheory/Integral/Prod.lean","source_sha256":"5b2267a5d7d2b8de1dd89ee6843bcfa63a8b7534535f7c92ebe17fe52a900c51","evidence":[{"path":"library/M007-0006/library-sources.json","sha256":"5345f180cc6820c5dcf40dba7457ce38a5f6efd074ea66eb0bb5a1a92c09be9f"}]}},{"id":"M009","kind":"mathlib","statement":"For a topological space X, a seminormed additive group Z, a set K⊂X and a map φ:X→Z, compactness of K and continuity of φ on K imply that there exists a real L such that |φ(z)|≤L for every z∈K.","source":{"declaration":"IsCompact.exists_bound_of_continuousOn","hypotheses":["X is topological and Z is a seminormed additive group.","K is compact.","φ is continuous on K."],"statement":"For a topological space X, a seminormed additive group Z, a set K⊂X and a map φ:X→Z, compactness of K and continuity of φ on K imply that there exists a real L such that |φ(z)|≤L for every z∈K.","module":"Mathlib.Analysis.Normed.Group.Bounded","signature":"@IsCompact.exists_bound_of_continuousOn : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {E : Type u_2} [inst : SeminormedAddGroup.{u_2} E] [inst_1 : TopologicalSpace.{u_1} α]
