{"id":"source-map.json","pointer":"/source_outputs","view":"value","value":{"N001":"For every x∈V and r>0, u(x,r)·u_t(x,r)=0 and u_t(x,r)·(u_tt(x,r)−Δu(x,r))=0. Moreover u(x,r)·u_tt(x,r)=−|u_t(x,r)|^2, and for every 1≤j≤n, u(x,r)·u_jj(x,r)=−|u_j(x,r)|^2. For every real a satisfying u_tt(x,r)−Δu(x,r)=a u(x,r), a=sum_{j=1}^n|u_j(x,r)|^2−|u_t(x,r)|^2; consequently u_tt−Δu=(sum_j|u_j|^2−|u_t|^2)u pointwise. No derivative of a is asserted or used.","N002":"For every t0>0 there exist a compact C⊂V and R>0 such that, with J=[t0/2,3t0/2] and Q=[−R,R]^n, C⊂(−R,R)^n, u(x,r)=q for x∉C and r∈J, and every positive-order coordinate partial derivative of u is zero on (V\C)×int J. For each r∈int J the sections of e,e_t,A,B_j,T_j,g_j and ∂_{x_j}g_j (1≤j≤n) are continuous, vanish outside C, have compact support, and are Lebesgue integrable on V. Each is bounded in absolute value on Q and its absolute integral is at most its bound times |Q|. The box Q is compact, measurable, has Lebesgue measure (2R)^n<∞, and C⊂int Q, so all these sections vanish on a neighborhood of ∂Q. In particular e(·,r) is integrable for every r>0.","N003":"The real functions e and g_j are jointly smooth on V×(0,∞). For every x∈V, r>0 and 1≤j≤n, ∂_r u_j(x,r)=u_jt(x,r), e_t(x,r)=2A(x,r)+2sum_{j=1}^n B_j(x,r), and ∂_{x_j}g_j(x,r)=B_j(x,r)+T_j(x,r). All the terms in these identities are continuous on the open domain.","N004":"For every t0>0 the actual finite integral E has derivative at t0, and E'(t0)=∫_V e_t(x,t0) dx. Thus E is differentiable on (0,∞).","N005":"For every t0>0 and every spatial index 1≤j≤n, all the following integrals are finite and ∫_V ∂_{x_j}g_j(x,t0) dx=0 and ∫_V B_j(x,t0) dx=−∫_V T_j(x,t0) dx; equivalently ∫_V u_j(x,t0)·u_jt(x,t0) dx=−∫_V u_t(x,t0)·u_jj(x,t0) dx.","P":"For every r>0 the function x↦e(x,r) is Lebesgue integrable on V; E is differentiable on (0,∞), and E'(r)=0 for every r>0. In particular E(s)=E(t) for all s,t>0. The energy is ∫_V (|u_t|^2+sum_{j=1}^n|u_j|^2) dx, with no factor 1/2 and no assertion at time zero."},"has_more":false,"next_offset":null}
