{"id": "nl0.json", "pointer": "/propositions/7", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "M002", "kind": "mathlib", "statement": "For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed additive commutative groups X,Z with normed 𝕜-vector-space structures, map φ:X→Z, point z∈X and smoothness order ℓ∈WithTop(N∞): if φ is C^ℓ at z and minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ, then its second Fréchet derivative is symmetric: for all v,w∈X, D(Dφ)(z)[v][w]=D(Dφ)(z)[w][v]. The minimum smoothness is 2 when the field has IsRCLikeNormedField (a real- or complex-like normed field) and analytic order ω otherwise; D denotes the total Fréchet derivative, zero when no derivative exists.", "definitions": [], "binders": [{"symbol": "𝕜", "type": "nontrivially normed field"}, {"symbol": "X", "type": "normed additive commutative group and normed 𝕜-space"}, {"symbol": "Z", "type": "normed additive commutative group and normed 𝕜-space"}, {"symbol": "φ", "type": "map X→Z"}, {"symbol": "z", "type": "point of X"}, {"symbol": "ℓ", "type": "element of WithTop(N∞)"}, {"symbol": "v", "type": "vector in X"}, {"symbol": "w", "type": "vector in X"}], "objects": ["𝕜", "X", "Z", "φ", "z", "ℓ", "v", "w"], "source": {"declaration": "ContDiffAt.isSymmSndFDerivAt", "hypotheses": ["The field and both normed spaces have the stated structures.", "φ is C^ℓ at z.", "minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ."], "module": "Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.FDeriv.Symmetric", "signature": "@ContDiffAt.isSymmSndFDerivAt : ∀ {𝕜 : Type u_1} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField.{u_1} 𝕜] {E : Type u_2} {F : Type u_3}
  [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup.{u_2} E] [inst_2 : NormedSpace.{u_1, u_2} 𝕜 E] [inst_3 : NormedAddCommGroup.{u_3} F]
  [inst_4 : NormedSpace.{u_1, u_3} 𝕜 F] {f : E → F} {x : E} {n : WithTop.{0} ℕ∞},
  ContDiffAt.{u_1, u_2, u_3} 𝕜 n f x → LE.le.{0} (minSmoothness.{u_1} 𝕜 2) n → IsSymmSndFDerivAt.{u_1, u_2, u_3} 𝕜 f x", "declaration_kind": "theorem", "mathlib_commit": "905b95818eb32af7874a58b427f50c1711a5e96c", "source_path": "Mathlib/Analysis/Calculus/FDeriv/Symmetric.lean", "source_sha256": "c262fa67a6097d95f55ef053fb2870a9b84b097f21c8cfea65b46e6d1677d725", "evidence": [{"path": "library/M002-0001/library-sources.json", "sha256": "69fb653c43a766c0d13ab081230621ee5d1e2569bcf1c9c6c283276fed01e642"}], "statement": "For any nontrivially normed field 𝕜, normed additive commutative groups X,Z with normed 𝕜-vector-space structures, map φ:X→Z, point z∈X and smoothness order ℓ∈WithTop(N∞): if φ is C^ℓ at z and minSmoothness(𝕜,2)≤ℓ, then its second Fréchet derivative is symmetric: for all v,w∈X, D(Dφ)(z)[v][w]=D(Dφ)(z)[w][v]. The minimum smoothness is 2 when the field has IsRCLikeNormedField (a real- or complex-like normed field) and analytic order ω otherwise; D denotes the total Fréchet derivative, zero when no derivative exists."}}, "has_more": false, "next_offset": null}

