{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R004/16", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG017", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "fact": "The real constant K is integrable on Q with respect to dx restricted to Q.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inputs/0/statement", "reason": "N002 gives dx(Q)<∞."}, {"location": "/inference/argument/2/text", "reason": "K=max(L,0) is a finite real number."}], "justification": "MeasureTheory.integrableOn_const applies: dx(Q)≠∞ and the extended norm of the finite real K is not infinity. This does not assume the constant function is integrable on all of V.", "kind": "mathlib", "source": {"declaration": "MeasureTheory.integrableOn_const", "module": "Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntegrableOn", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.integrableOn_const : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {ε' : Type u_4} {mα : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {s : Set.{u_1} α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α}
