{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R004/17", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG018", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "fact": "β=K1_Q, equivalently Q.indicator(fun _↦K), is integrable on V.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inputs/0/statement", "reason": "Q is measurable and has finite measure."}, {"location": "/inference/argument/3/text", "reason": "β is the indicator constant; BG017 proves integrability of K on Q."}], "justification": "MeasureTheory.integrable_indicator_iff transports exactly that integrability on Q to integrability of β on V, with the required measurable-set hypothesis.", "kind": "mathlib", "source": {"declaration": "MeasureTheory.integrable_indicator_iff", "module": "Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntegrableOn", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.integrable_indicator_iff : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {ε' : Type u_4} {mα : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {s : Set.{u_1} α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α}
