{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R004/21", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG020", "at": "/inference/argument/3/text", "fact": "For every fixed y∈V, Φ(ζ,y) tends through punctured-zero real increments to e_t(y,t0).", "grounds": [{"location": "/inputs/1/statement", "reason": "e is smooth at positive times; BG008 identifies its temporal derivative."}, {"location": "/definitions/9/definition", "reason": "e_t is the actual derivative of the temporal section."}], "justification": "hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero applied over R to the temporal section at t0 yields this limit, using the derivative e_t checked in BG008. Extend the section by zero outside positive times; because η=t0/4<t0, this extension agrees with e on all relevant increments, and Φ equals its quotient whenever 0<|ζ|<η. This is the elementary derivative characterization bridge, not an integrated limit exchange.", "kind": "mathlib", "source": {"declaration": "hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero", "module": "Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Slope", "signature": "@hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero : ∀ {𝕜 : Type u} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField.{u} 𝕜] {F : Type v} [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup.{v} F]
