{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R004/22", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG023", "at": "/inference/argument/5/text", "kind": "mathlib", "fact": "The punctured-zero limit of the actual energy quotient obtained in S006 proves HasDerivAt E (∫_V e_t(y,t0)dy) t0, hence the derivative claimed in N004.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inference/argument/4/text", "reason": "F004 proves the limit of the integrals of Φ."}, {"location": "/inference/argument/5/text", "reason": "M013 and M014 identify these integrals with the energy quotient for 0<|ζ|<η."}, {"location": "/inputs/0/statement", "reason": "N002 supplies the integrability guard for the actual E, and η=t0/4 makes both times positive."}], "justification": "Apply the reverse implication of hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero to any extension of E outside (0,∞). Its local quotient equals the displayed one near zero. The local derivative on the open positive-time domain is independent of that extension. No new limit is asserted: the necessary limit was already established by M004 and the exact integral identity.", "source": {"declaration": "hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero", "module": "Mathlib.Analysis.Calculus.Deriv.Slope", "signature": "@hasDerivAt_iff_tendsto_slope_zero : ∀ {𝕜 : Type u} [inst : NontriviallyNormedField.{u} 𝕜] {F : Type v} [inst_1 : NormedAddCommGroup.{v} F]
