{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R005/19", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG022", "at": "/inference/argument/2/text", "kind": "mathlib", "fact": "Every fixed-y derivative slice is integrable on all of R.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inputs/0/statement", "reason": "N002 supplies compact C and compact measurable Q with C contained in the open box, and all named sections continuous, integrable and zero outside C; t0 lies in int J."}, {"location": "/inference/locals", "reason": "Xhat is a finite product of real lines, χ is coordinate restriction and its inverse coordinate insertion; t0>0 and 1≤j≤n."}], "justification": "Its support is contained in (−R,R) by F001 and the coordinate test in BG001, hence in (−R,R]. Interval integrability BG019 is integrability on that half-open set by M006's explicit convention. The probed support-subset equivalence therefore gives global integrability; the codomain R has the required normed and metrizable structures.", "source": {"declaration": "MeasureTheory.integrableOn_iff_integrable_of_support_subset", "module": "Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntegrableOn", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.integrableOn_iff_integrable_of_support_subset : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {mα : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α} {s : Set.{u_1} α} {μ : MeasureTheory.Measure.{u_1} α} {ε' : Type u_7}
