{"id": "background-supplement.json", "pointer": "/notes/R005/21", "view": "value", "value": {"id": "BG024", "at": "/inference/argument/1/text", "kind": "mathlib", "fact": "The product of identity on Xhat and evaluation on the singleton j block preserves their product measures.", "grounds": [{"location": "/inference/locals", "reason": "Xhat is a finite product of real lines, χ is coordinate restriction and its inverse coordinate insertion; t0>0 and 1≤j≤n."}, {"location": "/inputs/7/statement", "reason": "M017 supplies the singleton evaluation measurable equivalence and its measure-preservation property."}, {"location": "/inputs/4/statement", "reason": "M011 supplies the coordinate split into the other-index and singleton-index product blocks."}], "justification": "M017 applies because j lies in {1,...,n}, so the second index subtype has the unique element j. Identity preserves its measure directly. BG006–BG007 supply s-finiteness of the two source factors required by the checked MeasurePreserving.prod.", "source": {"declaration": "MeasureTheory.MeasurePreserving.prod", "module": "Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Prod", "signature": "@MeasureTheory.MeasurePreserving.prod : ∀ {α : Type u_1} {β : Type u_2} {γ : Type u_3} [inst : MeasurableSpace.{u_1} α] [inst_1 : MeasurableSpace.{u_2} β]
